    "post_decision_tracking": "Exit IC memo recommending the Investment Committee approve the sale of Precision Asset Inspections, Inc. to Bureau Veritas S.A. for $310M enterprise value (10.0x LTM Adj. EBITDA of $31.0M). Atlas Crossing Partners Fund II invested $48M in equity (Jan 2016 platform + 3 bolt-ons) and generated estimated total proceeds of $171M including escrow release, yielding a 3.0x gross MOIC and ~23.8% gross IRR over a 5.9-year hold. The company grew revenue from $52M to $142M and EBITDA from $9.4M to $31.0M, completed 3 geographic bolt-ons, commercialized the Vantage IQ SaaS platform to $8.2M ARR, and expanded recurring revenue from 38% to 68%. Bureau Veritas was selected from three final bids as highest value, all-cash with fastest close, with CEO and CTO rolling 4% of EV into the BV vehicle."
